{"summary": "Steering sprint on N1 (closed vocabulary): the Shaper proposed a major overhaul replacing free identifiers/strings with typed ontology categories (entity/role/value/attribute/operation/intent symbols), atomic literals, and structured code nodes, fully complying with the note. The Critic found the direction sound but ruled needs-rework because membership rules only checked namespace prefixes rather than actual glossary entries, VALUE was too broad to preserve N3 distinctions, arbitrary-text COMMENT still violated N4, URL validity relied on external RFC-3986 (violating N5), and op_find's result type and most operation/intent schemas remained underspecified, causing most sampled real-world tasks (cart actions, SWE-bench reports, recipes, meal plans, medical/persona requests) to have no valid encoding. The decisive evidence was the batch of failed simulations (e.g. shopping-cart, SWE-bench django/sympy, PRISM/PATHs open requests) showing the closed vocabulary is still too sparse and its membership/schema rules too loose to satisfy N1-N5 and N7 together."}

